{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"densely. Made by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inducedSubgraph(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spanningSubgraph(edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph(vertices:edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraph_view"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsSubgraph"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SubDigraph"},{"type":"text","text":", Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"filtered_graph"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations"]]},"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView.swift#L29","fileName":"SubgraphView.swift"},"title":"SubgraphView","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:15GraphOperations12SubgraphViewV","symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"GraphOperations"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertices","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" are the kept vertices in the base’s order, at view indices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":": the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"view keeps two arrays, base index to view index and back, so a row is the base’s row filtered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and renumbered with one array load per entry and no hashing. A spanning subgraph keeps every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex at its base index."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges"}]},{"type":"text","text":" keep the base’s positions, so a weight closure keyed by the base’s positions works"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the view. An edge is in the view when both its ends are, and, if an edge set was given,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when it is in the set. With an edge set the view has dense edge indices: an edge’s index is its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rank among the kept edges in base order. Over a base with edge indices the set is a bit mask"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a count per 64-bit word, so the rank costs one popcount. Over a base without them (an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", a complement, an induced subgraph) the set is the sorted kept positions, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a row entry or a rank costs a binary search. An induced subgraph has no edge indices: building"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its edge mask would cost O(m). One on every vertex keeps the base’s rows, edge indices and flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rows."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The view holds a copy of the base (value semantics), so mutating the original never shows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through. Phase 1 needs a base with vertex indices; a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" with vertex holes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"traps at construction."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView"},"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges"],"anchor":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"references":{"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/UndirectedEdges":{"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Base"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/undirectededges","title":"SubgraphView.UndirectedEdges","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedEdges"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedEdges"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The edges of an undirected "},{"code":"SubgraphView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the kept edges of the base, in its order, at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its positions."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementations","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph-implementations"},"doc://GraphOperations/s8CopyableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Copyable","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP"},"doc://GraphOperations/s9EscapableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Escapable"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"DirectedGraph","abstract":[{"text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/EdgeRow":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EdgeRow","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EdgeRow","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/edgerow","type":"topic","title":"SubgraphView.EdgeRow","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A row of positions (out-, in- or incident edges): the base’s, with the dropped edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"skipped. The index row is stepped in step only when the view drops vertices."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/EdgeIndexRow":{"title":"SubgraphView.EdgeIndexRow","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/edgeindexrow","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EdgeIndexRow","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EdgeIndexRow","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The view’s edge indices of a row of positions: each kept position’s rank, or the base’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own edge-index row when the view keeps every vertex and every edge."}]},"doc://GraphOperations/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/base":{"title":"base","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/base","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"base"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Base"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The graph the view filters.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations","type":"topic","title":"GraphOperations","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/DirectedGraph-Implementations":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/directedgraph-implementations","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[],"title":"DirectedGraph Implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedGraph-Implementations","type":"topic"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/DirectedEdges":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedEdges"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The edges of a directed "},{"code":"SubgraphView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the kept edges of the base, in its order, at its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions. Stepping from one to the next skips the dropped ones."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","title":"SubgraphView.DirectedEdges","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/directededges","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Base","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}]},"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedEdges"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"densely. Made by "},{"code":"inducedSubgraph(on:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"spanningSubgraph(edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"subgraph(vertices:edges:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (NetworkX’s "},{"code":"subgraph_view","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", JGraphT’s "},{"code":"AsSubgraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"SubDigraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", Boost’s "},{"code":"filtered_graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView","title":"SubgraphView","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubgraphView"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/Graph-Implementations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/Graph-Implementations","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/graph-implementations","title":"Graph Implementations"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/BidirectionalDirectedGraph":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","abstract":[{"text":"A directed graph that also answers in-neighborhoods: Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"BidirectionalGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Kept apart","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" because in-adjacency usually costs extra storage, and many algorithms only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"go forward.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"Graph","abstract":[{"text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"between them. Kept apart from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one, and no type is both. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directed"},{"text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/SubgraphView/IndexRow":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IndexRow","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A row in index space (successors, predecessors or neighbors): the base’s row with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dropped entries skipped and the rest renumbered. One array load per entry, no hashing. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row holds one reference to the view’s renumbering and edge set (none when the view keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"everything), and walks the base’s position row only under an edge set.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview\/indexrow","title":"SubgraphView.IndexRow","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IndexRow","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphOperations/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype"}}}